            "review_title": "Review at Vietnamese Pancake Ngoc Son Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Johnny Novo\nNew York City, New York337 contributions\n0\nBanh Xeo\nApr 2024 • Friends\nThis was my introduction to Banh Xeo, which is essentially a stuffed Vietnamese pancake… and boy is it STUFFED like a Thanksgiving turkey, or like LeBron on Iguodala. \n\nThank GOD we came with some locals, as I would have had no idea how to eat it ahahha. You essentially rip part of the pancake off while making sure you get some shrimp and meat, roll it up in the lettuce, add some leaves and spices, dip it in the fish sauce, and demolish it.\n\nThis thing was ENORMOUS too, and for the low price of 65,000 Dong ($2.60 USD) it's crazy bang for your buck. I mean the whole country is but I feel bad about that sometimes, idk. \n\nIt was delicious. I’ve never tasted anything like it. That’s what's so great about traveling though. You learn so much so fast… If I did have to compare though I’d almost liken it to a crepe as opposed to a pancake… eh but the crepe comparison isn’t that great either. Idk. If you’re in Vietnam you need to try this.\n\nIG @jnov_\nTiktok @jnov_reviews\nRead more\nWritten April 7, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
